From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fe13 <engine@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 03:32:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/21] frontend: Fire Emblem: Awakening's top-screen extras,
 per game, off by default

For a game the extras know (Fire Emblem: Awakening, EUR and USA), its own
settings window gets "Top-screen extras", all off unless ticked:

- Battle UI: None (default, as the top screen alone always showed),
  Vanilla style (the bottom screen's battle panels over the top one) or
  FE3H style (banners whose text is read off the bottom screen).
- Bottom screen over the top one: E on the keyboard or the left stick's
  click on a controller (settings.toml bottom_over_key / bottom_over_button)
  shows the bottom screen over the middle of the top one, with the game's own
  open and close sounds; again, or B, hides it. A stick steers a pointer on
  it, A touches. The title screen's prompt and the world map's place name show
  over the top screen too.
- Touch pointer: the battle's buttons show over the top screen on a press and
  take mouse clicks; the mouse pointer hides after three seconds still.

They work while Screens is "Top screen only" and the rotation upright; the
game's screens are watched only while one is on (Config::game_screens).
Nothing is saved for other games, and the general settings get only the two
bindings.

Adapted from fe-awakening-recomp 832fe86 (github.com/Zelkin1/fe-awakening-recomp,
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 the authors of the Fire Emblem: Awakening
recompilation project): overlays.rs, banners.rs and sounds.rs (taken whole;
sounds.rs gets a USA entry), the App logic in lib.rs, the BattleUi setting,
Audio::play, Gamepads::lean and gui::BOTTOM_SCREEN. Left out: its map
overview on Select and scripted taps, "original" mode, launcher theme,
Update Launcher, console window, folder/file chooser changes, the speed
slider and every changed default (pad A/B, 16:9, fullscreen, enhancements
on, forced GPU drawing and recompiled code). Its default controller button,
ZR's trigger, is ZR in Zakuro 0.2.32, so the left stick's click is used.
